content.content:
   be its own descendant) and silently dropped this fallback, leaving
   --nx-chrome undefined on any portal page without an active banner. */
--nx-chrome: 0px;
body.nx-has-banner { --nx-chrome: 28px; }

/* The shell and its sidebar are sized against the viewport, but they do not
   START at the top of it when something sits above them in flow. A bare
   `min-h-dvh`/`h-dvh` then makes the document exactly --nx-chrome taller than
   the window — the app frame can fit its own content perfectly and the page
   still scrolls by the height of the banner. */
.nx-shell-root { min-height: calc(100dvh - var(--nx-chrome)); }
.nx-shell-rail { height: calc(100dvh - var(--nx-chrome)); }

/* ── Preloader ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   The route-segment loading state (components/nx/Preloader). CSS-only on
   purpose: it is on screen precisely while the page's own JavaScript is not
   ready, so it cannot depend on any. Every animated property returns to its
   starting value at 100%, which is what makes the loop seamless rather than
   snapping back on repeat.

   Sized against --nx-chrome, same as .nx-shell-root/.nx-appframe. It used to
   be a bare `min-h-[68vh]` Tailwind class — 68% of the true viewport height,
   with no idea that the sandbox banner and the sticky header already sit
   above it in flow. On the sandbox that extra ~28px plus the header was
   sometimes enough to push the whole document past 100dvh, so the page
   scrolled and the mark centred itself in a box taller than the visible
   area instead of the viewport. */
.nx-pre { min-height: calc(68dvh - var(--nx-chrome)); }




.nx-pre-halo {
  position: absolute; inset: 6px; border-radius: 999px;
  background: radial-gradient(circle, rgba(79,124,255,0.55), rgba(63,188,216,0.22) 45%, transparent 70%);
  filter: blur(12px);
  animation: nx-pre-halo 2.4s ease-in-out infinite;
}
/* A conic sweep masked down to a hairline ring — one element, no SVG arc
   maths, and it rotates on the compositor. */
.nx-pre-ring {
  position: absolute; inset: 0; border-radius: 999px;
  background: conic-gradient(from 0deg,
    transparent 0 58%,
    rgba(24,224,194,0.85) 72%,
    rgba(95,208,255,0.95) 84%,
    rgba(162,59,255,0.9) 94%,
    transparent 100%);
  -webkit-mask: radial-gradient(farthest-side, transparent calc(100% - 2.5px), #000 calc(100% - 2.5px));
  mask: radial-gradient(farthest-side, transparent calc(100% - 2.5px), #000 calc(100% - 2.5px));
  animation: nx-pre-spin 1.5s linear infinite;
}
.nx-pre-slab { animation: nx-pre-slab 1.5s ease-in-out infinite; }
.nx-pre-rail {
  position: relative; display: block; overflow: hidden;
  width: 132px; height: 2px; border-radius: 999px;
  background: rgba(120,170,255,0.14);
}
.nx-pre-bar {
  position: absolute; inset-block: 0; left: 0; width: 22%;
  border-radius: 999px;
  background: linear-gradient(90deg, transparent, #5fd0ff, #a23bff, transparent);
  animation: nx-pre-bar 1.5s cubic-bezier(.55,0,.35,1) infinite;
}
/* Reduced motion: hold the mark lit and still. A loading state that cannot
   move must still read as "working", so the ring stays visible rather than
   the whole thing disappearing. */
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  .nx-pre-halo, .nx-pre-ring, .nx-pre-slab, .nx-pre-bar { animation: none; }
  .nx-pre-slab { opacity: 1; }
  .nx-pre-bar { width: 100%; background: linear-gradient(90deg, #5fd0ff, #a23bff); }
}

/* ══ VPS command centre ══════════════════════════════════════════════
   The panel uses `.card .card-glass` with a per-instance `--tone`, exactly
   as SupportView and WhatsNewView do. It does NOT define its own surface.

   Three passes here built a parallel glass treatment — fills, outer blooms,
   a colour field behind the grid — while `.card-glass` already existed as the
   owner's own spec, itself rebuilt three times against direct corrections
   ("only inner glow, no outer glow", "the radius is too big", "no colour
   filled inside the card"). Re-deriving it was how this panel drifted out of
   step with the rest of the product. Anything below is only what `.card-glass`
   does not cover. */

/* Bare glowing icon — no plate behind it. */
.nxp-ico { filter: drop-shadow(0 0 9px currentColor); }

/* Segmented control with a sliding thumb (--n count, --i active index). */
/* inline-GRID with equal columns, not inline-flex. With flex the container
   hugs its content, so `flex-1` had no free space to distribute and the items
   kept their natural widths ("All" narrow, "Network" wide) while the thumb
   below assumed they were equal — which is why the highlight sat across two
   options. Equal grid columns make the thumb's arithmetic true. */
.nxp-seg { position: relative; display: inline-grid; grid-auto-flow: column;
           grid-auto-columns: 1fr; padding: 3px; border-radius: 11px;
           border: 1px solid rgba(150,195,255,.16); background: rgba(10,22,48,.44); }
.nxp-seg::before {
  content: ""; position: absolute; top: 3px; bottom: 3px; left: 3px;
  width: calc((100% - 6px) / var(--n));
  transform: translateX(calc(var(--i) * 100%));
  border-radius: 9px;
  background: linear-gradient(120deg, rgba(110,70,240,.9), rgba(56,120,240,.78));
  box-shadow: inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255,255,255,.35);
  transition: transform .26s cubic-bezier(.34,1.2,.5,1);
}
.nxp-seg > * { position: relative; z-index: 1; }

/* Status dot that breathes while live. */
.nxp-live { position: relative; }
.nxp-live::after {
  content: ""; position: absolute; inset: -5px; border-radius: 999px;
  border: 1px solid currentColor; opacity: .55;
  animation: nxp-ping 2.6s cubic-bezier(0,0,.2,1) infinite;
}

.nxp-skel { position: relative; overflow: hidden; border-radius: 10px; background: rgba(120,170,255,.09); }
.nxp-skel::after {
  content: ""; position: absolute; inset: 0;
  background: linear-gradient(90deg, transparent, rgba(150,195,255,.14), transparent);
  transform: translateX(-100%); animation: nxp-sheen 1.5s ease-in-out infinite;
}

.nxp-backdrop { animation: nxp-fade .18s ease-out both; backdrop-filter: blur(8px); }
.nxp-modal    { animation: nxp-in .22s cubic-bezier(.34,1.3,.56,1) both; }


.nxp-draw { stroke-dasharray: 1400; stroke-dashoffset: 1400; animation: nxp-trace 1.1s ease-out forwards; }

@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  .nxp-live::after, .nxp-skel::after { animation: none; }

