     These used to be bare rules in the layer above, winning everywhere
     (marketing/login/admin included) purely by appearing later in the file.
     Moved here, under the has() scope, so production's own .card/.glass/
     .btn-* definitions above are what marketing/login/admin actually get. */


  .card {
    @apply rounded-[12px] border p-6;
    border-color: var(--color-rim);
    background: var(--color-surface);
    box-shadow: 0 10px 30px -18px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.9);
    /* Production's restored bare .card (this same file, "Surfaces" section)
       carries `backdrop-blur-md` — a real backdrop-filter, which a rule at
       higher specificity doesn't implicitly clear just by winning on OTHER
       properties (background/border here). Left in place, ANY `.card` inside
       the portal becomes a new containing block for `position: fixed`
       descendants — which is exactly what broke full-screen modals nested
       inside one (the support "New ticket" dialog rendered pinned to its
       parent card instead of the viewport). Nexion's own card was never
       meant to blur what's behind it (it's a solid gradient fill) — this
       just has to say so explicitly to actually cancel the inherited value. */
    backdrop-filter: none;
  }
  .card-hover {
    @apply transition-colors duration-200;
  }
  .card-hover:hover {
    border-color: var(--color-rim-hi);
